Ah yes, it is also the only way to pick up stuff that the game stupidly
places on the traps themselves.  That may be why it is not punished.

But thinking about that, I realized one more unpunished breach of the
rules of original Sokoban.  You can dig a new pit and push a boulder into
it.  It wouldn't help if you've already locked a boulder, but it could
simplify the puzzle if you do it early, since the vanilla Sokoban levels
include more boulders than you need.

Digging a new pit in Sokoban has a legitimate use -- obtaining buried
items that may have originally been placed on the first trap.  In the
harder level 2, and both level 1s, you must fill that trap before you can
step on that grid.


Both of these non-puzzle-cheating uses could be averted if the game
considered the traps ineligible for random item placement.

